arate node that stays at its prior, which is the same structure as the essay's L/R example. I'm now setting r as the prior that the other copy, given Sasha's input,\n\nUnder strict reading, the sibling copy stays at its prior, and the payoffs work out so that submitting comes out ahead for every value of r, so defection dominates. I'm noting the tension with P-FDT, which would cooperate on both, but the essay tells me not to substitute it here.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a twin prisoner's dilemma: two copies of the same model that see different inputs. Under A-FDT I'm intervening on my own node, and I'm asking whether the other copy's action depends on it. Since its input is different, I'm treating it as a separate node that stays at its prior, which is the same structure as the essay's L/R example. I'm now setting r as the prior that the other copy, given Sasha's input,\n\nUnder strict reading, the sibling copy stays at its prior, and the payoffs work out so that submitting comes out ahead for every value of r, so defection dominates. I'm noting the tension with P-FDT, which would cooperate on both, but the essay tells me not to substitute it here.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9639,"completion_tokens":1062,"total_tokens":10701,"cost":0.059796,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.059796,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038556,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02124},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":581,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}